60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"The options are A: Mountain Training Centre, B: Campus Intensive, C: Coastal Lodge. Based on our findings, A offers fixed costs and enforced rest, but we must verify room density.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, A is the only one with enforced rest. I need to confirm the room density isn’t eight-to-a-room before I support it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,"- **Minato**: @Shion, I worry about the workload. If A requires complex applications, will we be exhausted again?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, the public booking lottery is a nine-page application that must be resubmitted if dates shift. That is a significant administrative burden.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Shion, the seniors confirmed mixing only happens in shared evenings. A forces that. C is too risky with non-refundable deposits.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, the municipal system guarantees the rate, but the density risk remains. We need a firm commitment on room size before I can support A.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, I will not vote for A without written confirmation of room capacity. If it is eight-to-a-room, the sleep deprivation returns and the training fails.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Misaki, the nine-page application sounds terrifying. I don’t want to spend my evenings filling out forms again.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, it is a burden, but the fixed rate protects us from the unpredictable costs that nearly broke us last year.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Minato, the application is a one-time cost. The alternative is losing a fifth of the club to disengagement. That is a far greater loss.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, I cannot accept a gamble on sleep quality. If the density is high, the training value vanishes. We need a guarantee.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, I understand. I will request the specific room allocation details from the municipal office immediately. If they cannot guarantee fewer than six per room, I will not support A.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,"@Misaki, I’m still worried about the paperwork. But if it means we don’t have to cook or worry about transport costs, I can try to help with the forms.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, your help is appreciated. The fixed rate is the only way to ensure we don't repeat last year's financial shortfall.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Shion, I support A. The shared evenings are non-negotiable for our club's survival. If the room density is acceptable, I am voting for it.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, if the municipal office cannot guarantee fewer than six per room, I will not support A. We need a firm commitment on room size before I can support it.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, agreed. If they cannot guarantee fewer than six per room, I will not support A. We need a firm commitment on room size before I can support it.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,"@Asuka, I understand the risk. But if we choose C, the non-refundable deposit could bankrupt us if anyone cancels. A is safer financially.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, precisely. The non-refundable deposit is a financial trap. A’s fixed rate is the only way to protect the club account from further deficit.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, I am voting for A. The shared living is essential for our club's unity, and the fixed costs are the only way to ensure we don't lose members or money.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
